<title>UGANDA: Uganda urges support for coffee price support move.</title>
<headline>Uganda urges support for coffee price support move.</headline>
<dateline>KAMPALA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uganda called on leading coffee producing countries to support moves to boost prices.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to convince producers to cut exports for the prices to go up,&quot; state minister for trade and industry Abel Rwendeire told reporters on Monday. &quot;We need to lobby producers to cut exports.&quot;</p>
<p>Rwendeire was speaking on his return from the annual conference of the Inter-Africa Coffee Organisation in Abidjan.</p>
<p>Uganda, Angola and Ivory Coast now make up a committee created at the Abidjan meeting to lobby key producers such as Brazil on cutting exports.</p>
<p>The minister gave no details on the percentage of stocks he wanted major producers to withhold or whether a formal meeting with such producers would be called.</p>
<p>--Nairobi Newsroom +254-2 330-261</p>
</text>
